{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state graph (computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than imperative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a native SwiftUI construct maps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a helper — for example the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Interaction patch’s four discrete output ports, or Drag’s momentum + rubber-band"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics — Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it."}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"title":"Reference"},{"anchor":"Helpers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"],"title":"Helpers"},{"anchor":"Examples","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/TouchOrigamiExampleView"],"title":"Examples"},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/SwiftUICore"],"title":"Extended Modules","generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"co